  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array AAA of length NNN, and an integer KKK.\n\nAAA is said to be a nice array if there exists an array BBB of length NNN satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\nFor every index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), Bi=⌊AiK⌋B_i = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{A_i}{K} \\right\\rfloorBi​=⌊KAi​​⌋, or Bi=⌈AiK⌉B_i = \\left\\lceil \\frac{A_i}{K} \\right\\rceilBi​=⌈KAi​​⌉; and\nB1+B2+…+BN=0B_1 + B_2 + \\ldots + B_N = 0B1​+B2​+…+BN​=0.\nIs AAA a nice array?\n\nNote that ⌊&nbsp;&nbsp;⌋\\left\\lfloor \\ \\ \\right\\rfloor⌊&nbsp;&nbsp;⌋ and ⌈&nbsp;&nbsp;⌉\\left\\lceil \\ \\ \\right\\rceil⌈&nbsp;&nbsp;⌉ denote the floor and ceiling functions, respectively.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of array AAA and the division parameter.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line a single string denoting the answer: `\"YES\"` if AAA is a nice array, and `\"NO\"` otherwise (without quotes).\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e., the strings `NO`, `No`, `nO`, and `no` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\le K \\le 10^91≤K≤109",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "It's guaranteed that the sum of NNN across all tests won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n4 2\n2 4 -2 -4\n2 3\n5 -6\n2 1\n-1 2\n2 2\n-1 2",
        "output": "YES\nYES\nNO\nYES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choose B=[1,2,−1,2]B = [1, 2, -1, 2]B=[1,2,−1,2], which satisfies Bi=⌊AiK⌋B_i = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{A_i}{K} \\right\\rfloorBi​=⌊KAi​​⌋ for all iii. The sum of this array is 000, so AAA is nice.\nTest case 333: No valid BBB exists, so AAA isn't nice.\nTest case 444: B=[−1,1]B = [-1, 1]B=[−1,1] is a valid array, so AAA is nice."
      }
    ]
